1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,503
COME ON, JOEY.

2
00:00:02,544 --> 00:00:04,421
I TOLD YOU EVERYTHING
I KNEW LAST NIGHT.

3
00:00:04,463 --> 00:00:05,756
IT'S NOT THAT BIG A DEAL.

4
00:00:05,798 --> 00:00:07,341
SO MONICA AND CHANDLER
ARE DOING IT.

5
00:00:07,382 --> 00:00:11,136
I CANNOT BELIEVE
YOU WOULD SAY THAT.

6
00:00:11,178 --> 00:00:15,056
SORRY. MONICA AND CHANDLER
ARE "MAKING LOVE."

7
00:00:15,098 --> 00:00:16,642
NO, I MEAN, COME ON

8
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:19,436
THIS IS A HUGE DEAL.

9
00:00:19,478 --> 00:00:21,062
COME ON, I NEED
MORE DETAILS.

10
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:23,064
LIKE, WHO INITIATED
THE FIRST KISS?

11
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:24,566
I DON'T KNOW.

12
00:00:26,193 --> 00:00:28,445
IS HE ROMANTIC
WITH HER?

13
00:00:28,487 --> 00:00:29,780
I DON'T KNOW.

14
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,200
ARE THEY IN LOVE?

15
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:34,994
I DON'T KNOW.

16
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:38,330
YOU DON'T KNOW ANYTHING.

17
00:00:38,372 --> 00:00:39,623
OH, I KNOW ONE THING.

18
00:00:39,665 --> 00:00:40,332
WHAT?

19
00:00:40,374 --> 00:00:41,041
THEY DID IT RIGHT THERE

20
00:00:41,082 --> 00:00:43,084
ON THE COUCH
YESTERDAY.

21
00:00:48,883 --> 00:00:53,846
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

22
00:00:53,888 --> 00:00:56,223
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

23
00:00:56,264 --> 00:00:59,184
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

24
00:00:59,226 --> 00:01:03,564
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

25
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:06,525
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

26
00:01:06,567 --> 00:01:08,569
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

27
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:12,197
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

28
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:14,324
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

29
00:01:14,366 --> 00:01:16,911
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

30
00:01:16,952 --> 00:01:19,162
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

31
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:22,374
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

32
00:01:22,416 --> 00:01:25,753
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

33
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:34,678
HEY, ROSS.

34
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:36,597
HEY.
YEAH.

35
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:38,390
HEY, GUNTHER,
COULD I HAVE
A SCONE, PLEASE?

36
00:01:38,432 --> 00:01:40,935
WANT TO HEAR SOME GOOD NEWS?

37
00:01:40,976 --> 00:01:42,770
SOMEONE I KNOW
IS GETTING MARRIED.

38
00:01:42,811 --> 00:01:44,897
YEAH, AND WEDDINGS
ARE HAPPY OCCASIONS.

39
00:01:44,939 --> 00:01:46,941
OH, BY-THE-BY,
IT'S MY EX-WIFE, EMILY.

40
00:01:46,982 --> 00:01:48,442
( all gasp )

41
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:49,860
I'M SORRY, MAN.

42
00:01:49,902 --> 00:01:50,861
HERE'S YOUR SCONE.

43
00:01:50,903 --> 00:01:51,904
THANKS, GUNTHER.

44
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:54,448
THANKS.

45
00:01:54,489 --> 00:01:56,992
STUPID BRITISH SNACK FOOD!

46
00:01:58,660 --> 00:01:59,954
DID THEY
TEACH YOU THAT

47
00:01:59,995 --> 00:02:01,830
IN YOUR ANGER
MANAGEMENT CLASS?

48
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:06,043
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT
MIGHT HELP YOU DEAL WITH IT?

49
00:02:06,085 --> 00:02:07,377
THINK OF IT THIS WAY...

50
00:02:07,419 --> 00:02:09,128
YOU AND EMILY ARE IN THE PAST.

51
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:11,214
AND YOU CAN'T BE MAD
ABOUT THE PAST.

52
00:02:11,256 --> 00:02:14,009
ARE YOU STILL MAD
ABOUT THE LOUISIANA PURCHASE?

53
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:17,345
I DON'T THINK
ANYBODY'S MAD
ABOUT THAT.

54
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:20,307
EXACTLY, BECAUSE
IT'S IN THE PAST.

55
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:26,187
ANYBODY
GOING TO EAT THAT?

56
00:02:29,775 --> 00:02:30,985
LOOK AT US,
ALL DRESSED UP

57
00:02:31,026 --> 00:02:32,152
FOR THE BIG
OFFICE PARTY.

58
00:02:32,193 --> 00:02:33,612
WHAT ARE WE
CELEBRATING?

59
00:02:33,654 --> 00:02:37,156
WE HAD LIQUOR LEFT OVER
FROM THE CHRISTMAS PARTY.

60
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:38,659
I THINK THIS
IS SO COOL.

61
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:39,660
NONE OF OUR FRIENDS
ARE HERE

62
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:40,661
SO WE CAN BE
A REAL COUPLE

63
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:41,954
WE DON'T
HAVE TO HIDE.

64
00:02:41,996 --> 00:02:43,664
I KNOW,
I CAN DO THIS.

65
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:44,915
OOH.

66
00:02:44,957 --> 00:02:46,500
AND I CAN DO THIS.

67
00:02:48,543 --> 00:02:50,587
Both:
WE CAN'T DO THAT, NO.

68
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:54,215
HEY, BING.

69
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:55,759
WHOA...
WHO'S THE PRETTY LADY

70
00:02:55,801 --> 00:02:57,970
AND WHAT THE HELL
IS SHE DOING WITH YOU?

71
00:02:58,012 --> 00:03:00,681
I ASK MYSELF
THAT VERY QUESTION, SIR.

72
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:01,807
THIS IS MONICA.

73
00:03:01,849 --> 00:03:03,142
THIS IS
MY BOSS, DOUG.

74
00:03:03,182 --> 00:03:04,810
DOUG, THIS IS MONICA.
NICE TO
MEET YOU.

75
00:03:04,852 --> 00:03:06,227
HI, THIS IS
MY WIFE, KARA.

76
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:07,604
NICE TO MEET
YOU, MONICA.

77
00:03:07,646 --> 00:03:09,188
BING!
OKAY.

78
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:11,399
HEY, BING, DID YOU HEAR
ABOUT THE NEW LAW FIRM

79
00:03:11,441 --> 00:03:12,567
WE GOT WORKING FOR US?

80
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:13,568
NO, SIR.

81
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:14,987
YEAH, DEWEY, CHEATEM
&amp; HOWE.

82
00:03:15,029 --> 00:03:19,366
( forced laugh )

83
00:03:19,407 --> 00:03:20,534
COME ON, HONEY

84
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,452
LET'S GO DRINK
OUR BODY WEIGHT, HUH?

85
00:03:22,494 --> 00:03:24,371
WHAT WAS THAT?

86
00:03:24,412 --> 00:03:25,372
WHAT?

87
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:26,707
THAT NOISE
YOU JUST MADE.

88
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:28,167
OH, THAT WAS
MY WORK LAUGH.

89
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:29,668
REALLY?
YOUR WORK LAUGH?

90
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:31,879
BELIEVE ME, IF YOU'RE GOING
TO SURVIVE THIS PARTY

91
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:34,048
YOU'RE GOING TO HAVE
TO COME UP WITH ONE, TOO.

92
00:03:34,089 --> 00:03:36,091
ALL RIGHT,
CHECK ME OUT.

93
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:37,467
OKAY.

94
00:03:37,509 --> 00:03:40,428
...HE SAYS, "$30, FATHER,
SAME AS IN TOWN."

95
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:43,306
( high pitched laugh )

96
00:03:47,019 --> 00:03:50,480
HEY, EVERYBODY AT WORK,
LOVED YOU LAST NIGHT.

97
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:51,272
REALLY?

98
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:52,357
AND THEY LIKE ME MORE

99
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:53,817
JUST BECAUSE
I WAS WITH YOU.

100
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:55,819
I THINK YOU REPAIRED
A LOT OF THE DAMAGE

101
00:03:55,861 --> 00:03:57,154
FROM WHEN THEY MET JOEY.

102
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:00,657
AND DOUG WANTS US
TO PLAY TENNIS WITH HIM.

103
00:04:00,699 --> 00:04:02,701
HE'S NEVER EVEN
TALKED TO ME
OUTSIDE OF WORK.

104
00:04:02,743 --> 00:04:05,037
EXCEPT FOR THAT
TIME WHEN WE BUMPED
INTO EACH OTHER

105
00:04:05,079 --> 00:04:06,663
AT THAT STRIP CLUB.

106
00:04:06,705 --> 00:04:09,083
STRIP... CHURCH.

107
00:04:11,001 --> 00:04:13,045
ANYWAY, I'M GOING
TO GO TRY TO
FIND A RACKET.

108
00:04:13,087 --> 00:04:14,004
I THOUGHT YOU HAD ONE.

109
00:04:14,046 --> 00:04:15,214
OH, I USED TO

110
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:17,174
BUT THEN JOEY THOUGHT
IT WOULD BE FUN

111
00:04:17,216 --> 00:04:18,466
TO GO TO CENTRAL PARK

112
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:20,219
AND HIT ROCKS
AT BIGGER ROCKS.

113
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:23,388
HEY, RACH,
DO YOU HAVE A TENNIS RACKET?

114
00:04:23,430 --> 00:04:24,639
OH, I LENT IT TO JOEY

115
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:26,391
AND I'VE NEVER ACTUALLY
GOTTEN IT BACK.

116
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:28,685
OKAY, GOOD LUCK WITH THAT.

117
00:04:31,939 --> 00:04:33,648
HEY, WHAT'S UP?
HEY.

118
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:35,192
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

119
00:04:35,234 --> 00:04:37,236
I THOUGHT YOU HAD TO DO
INVENTORY ALL DAY.

120
00:04:37,277 --> 00:04:38,695
WELL, YEAH, I DO.

121
00:04:38,737 --> 00:04:40,655
BUT, YOU KNOW, I DECIDED
I WOULD TAKE A LONG LUNCH

122
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:42,657
AND SPEND SOME TIME
WITH MY FRIEND, MONICA.

123
00:04:42,699 --> 00:04:46,369
YOU KNOW, I FEEL LIKE
WE DON'T TALK ANYMORE.

124
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:47,662
HOW ARE YOU?

125
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:49,831
WHAT IS
NEW WITH YOU?

126
00:04:49,873 --> 00:04:52,960
UM, NOT MUCH.

127
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:55,587
UH... WORK'S GOOD.

128
00:04:55,629 --> 00:04:57,714
OH, YOU KNOW, WE DON'T
HAVE TO TALK ABOUT WORK.

129
00:04:57,756 --> 00:04:58,966
WE CAN TALK
ABOUT ANYTHING.

130
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:01,551
OKAY, UM...

131
00:05:01,593 --> 00:05:03,220
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

132
00:05:03,262 --> 00:05:05,931
LET'S TALK ABOUT
RELATIONSHIPS.

133
00:05:05,973 --> 00:05:07,515
OKAY, WHAT'S
GOING ON WITH YOU?

134
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,434
NOTHING.

135
00:05:09,476 --> 00:05:11,145
YOU GO.

136
00:05:11,186 --> 00:05:13,021
WELL, THERE WAS THIS GUY

137
00:05:13,063 --> 00:05:15,690
AT THE BANK
THAT I THOUGHT WAS CUTE.

138
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:17,609
UM, BUT I DON'T ANYMORE.

139
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:20,654
WOW, THAT'S JUICY.

140
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:22,489
YOU KNOW WHAT,
THOUGH, MON?

141
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:25,117
I ACTUALLY DO
HAVE A LOT OF
WORK TO DO.

142
00:05:25,159 --> 00:05:28,703
SO, IF YOU'RE SURE THERE'S
JUST NOT ANYTHING ELSE...?

143
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:29,746
YES, I'M SURE.

144
00:05:29,788 --> 00:05:30,914
RACHEL,
IS THERE SOMETHING

145
00:05:30,956 --> 00:05:32,499
THAT YOU WANT
TO TALK TO ME ABOUT?

146
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:33,875
( sharply ):
NO.

147
00:05:36,461 --> 00:05:38,255
I...

148
00:05:38,297 --> 00:05:40,548
IF THERE WAS,
I WOULDN'T TELL YOU.

149
00:05:45,679 --> 00:05:48,431
( duck quacking )

150
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:49,766
OKAY, THEN WHAT HAPPENED?

151
00:05:49,808 --> 00:05:53,020
OH...

152
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:54,896
UH-HUH, UH-HUH.

153
00:05:54,938 --> 00:05:56,190
( chicken clucks )

154
00:05:56,231 --> 00:05:57,899
YOU'LL GET YOUR TURN.

155
00:05:57,941 --> 00:05:59,567
HEY, PHEEBS.
HEY.

156
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:00,861
WHAT'S GOING ON?
NOTHING.

157
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:02,487
THIS IS NOT OVER.

158
00:06:02,529 --> 00:06:04,363
NO, NO, NO.

159
00:06:04,405 --> 00:06:05,615
WHAT?

160
00:06:05,657 --> 00:06:06,908
I WAS UP ALL NIGHT

161
00:06:06,950 --> 00:06:09,536
WRITING THIS REALLY
NASTY LETTER TO EMILY.

162
00:06:09,577 --> 00:06:10,537
IT WAS PERFECT.

163
00:06:10,578 --> 00:06:12,539
AND NOW IT'S ALL COVERED IN...

164
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:14,875
ACTUALLY, THANKS.

165
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:17,376
ALL RIGHT, EVERYBODY
READY TO GO TO THE MOVIES?

166
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:20,172
UH, ACTUALLY I THINK
I'M GOING TO SKIP IT.

167
00:06:20,214 --> 00:06:21,548
REALLY?

168
00:06:21,589 --> 00:06:23,091
YEAH, I'M GOING
TO STAY AND
READ MY BOOK.

169
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:24,592
I JUST WANT TO
BE ALONE RIGHT NOW.

170
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:27,054
OH, SURE YOU
DON'T WANT TO COME?

171
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:28,763
TOM HANKS, MEG RYAN...

172
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:30,724
THEY GET MAIL AND STUFF.

173
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:32,767
THAT'S OKAY, JOE.

174
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:34,228
ALL RIGHT.

175
00:06:34,269 --> 00:06:35,729
( duck quacking )

176
00:06:38,148 --> 00:06:41,400
OOH... OH, GOD.

177
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:45,697
BING.

178
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:51,119
( screams )

179
00:06:51,161 --> 00:06:52,913
GAME.

180
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:56,124
WELL, I GOT TO
TELL YOU, BING.

181
00:06:56,166 --> 00:06:58,252
THAT PARTNER OF YOURS
IS A REAL TIGER.

182
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:01,296
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT,
SWEETHEART?

183
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:05,926
WE'RE JUST GOING TO GET
A LITTLE SIP OF WATER.

184
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:09,971
AM I ON FIRE TODAY,
OR WHAT?

185
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:12,599
THOSE BIRDS ARE BROWN, BASTED

186
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,726
AND READY TO BE CARVED.

187
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:17,396
OKAY... EASY, MARTINA.

188
00:07:19,022 --> 00:07:21,691
LISTEN, I THINK WE SHOULD
LET THEM WIN THE NEXT GAME.

189
00:07:21,733 --> 00:07:24,861
I'M SORRY, I DON'T
UNDERSTAND WHAT
YOU JUST SAID.

190
00:07:24,903 --> 00:07:27,281
LET THEM WIN ONE.

191
00:07:27,322 --> 00:07:28,489
ARE YOU CRAZY?

192
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,950
WE OWN THOSE TWO.

193
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:31,326
LOOK AT THEM.

194
00:07:31,368 --> 00:07:34,996
HE CAN'T EVEN BREATHE
AND SHE'S POPPIN' PILLS.

195
00:07:35,038 --> 00:07:37,791
YOU'RE NOT EVEN
GIVING THEM A CHANCE.

196
00:07:37,832 --> 00:07:39,500
THEY HAVE RACKETS,
DON'T THEY?

197
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:42,837
UH, BING, I THINK WE'RE

198
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,839
GOING TO MAKE THIS
THE LAST GAME.

199
00:07:44,881 --> 00:07:45,840
OH, YES, SIR.

200
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:47,008
PUT ME
OUT OF MY MISERY.

201
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:49,177
ARE YOU SURE
YOU NEVER PLAYED PRO?

202
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:51,179
PLEASE LET THEM WIN.

203
00:07:51,221 --> 00:07:52,680
I'LL TAKE IT
DOWN TO 95%

204
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:54,515
BUT THAT'S THE BEST
I CAN DO.

205
00:08:00,355 --> 00:08:01,648
OOPSEY, MISSED IT.

206
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:02,690
I GOT IT.

207
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:07,570
NICE SHOT.

208
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:18,081
I GOT IT.

209
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:21,251
LONG.

210
00:08:27,341 --> 00:08:29,550
I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU LET THEM WIN.

211
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:33,054
YEAH, AT LEAST YOU HID
YOUR FEELINGS WELL ABOUT IT.

212
00:08:33,096 --> 00:08:34,681
I WAS FRUSTRATED.

213
00:08:34,722 --> 00:08:35,849
IT WAS MY RACKET.

214
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,267
I WAS FRUSTRATED
WITH YOU.

215
00:08:37,309 --> 00:08:38,768
IF WE HADN'T
LOST THE GAME

216
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:40,645
THEY WOULD NEVER
HAVE INVITED US

217
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:42,022
TO DINNER TOMORROW NIGHT.

218
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:43,398
YOU KNOW WHAT
REALLY BOTHERS ME?

219
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:45,733
IT'S HOW DIFFERENT
YOU ACT AROUND THEM.

220
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:47,986
I MEAN, THE THROWING
THE TENNIS GAMES

221
00:08:48,028 --> 00:08:50,613
THE FAKE LAUGH,
THE "SEE YA
LATER, BING."

222
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:52,366
"NOT IF I SEE
YOU FIRST, DOUG."

223
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:55,535
"AH, AH, AH, AH!"

224
00:08:55,576 --> 00:08:56,370
I GOT TO TELL YOU

225
00:08:56,411 --> 00:08:57,496
I DON'T LIKE
"WORK CHANDLER."

226
00:08:57,536 --> 00:08:58,621
THE GUY'S A SUCK-UP.

227
00:08:58,663 --> 00:09:01,375
OKAY, BECAUSE
YOU SAID THAT

228
00:09:01,416 --> 00:09:04,294
I'M NOT
PUTTING OUT TONIGHT.

229
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:12,010
I'M TELLING YOU,
SOMETHING'S WRONG.

230
00:09:12,052 --> 00:09:13,803
MY BROTHER DOES NOT
STAY OUT ALL NIGHT.

231
00:09:13,845 --> 00:09:16,181
MAYBE WE SHOULD CHECK
THE TRASH CHUTE.

232
00:09:17,474 --> 00:09:20,143
ROSS COULDN'T FIT
DOWN THE TRASH CHUTE.

233
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:22,396
THAT'S RIGHT, HE ALMOST COULD.

234
00:09:22,437 --> 00:09:25,315
WHICH IS EXACTLY
HOW I GOT STUCK THERE.

235
00:09:26,441 --> 00:09:27,775
HEY.

236
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:30,320
OH, MY GOD.

237
00:09:30,362 --> 00:09:32,489
WHERE THE HELL
HAVE YOU BEEN?

238
00:09:32,531 --> 00:09:35,616
JUST...
YOU KNOW, OUT.

239
00:09:35,658 --> 00:09:36,617
OH... OUT.

240
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:38,203
OH, GOD,
I DON'T KNOW WHY

241
00:09:38,245 --> 00:09:40,247
WE DIDN'T THINK
TO CHECK THERE.

242
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:42,040
WHAT WERE YOU DOING?

243
00:09:42,082 --> 00:09:44,501
I, UH...
WENT TO A BAR.

244
00:09:44,543 --> 00:09:49,089
AND THEN I JUST WALKED AROUND
FOR A WHILE.

245
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:50,589
YOU WALK AROUND
ALL NIGHT

246
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:52,133
IN THE CITY
BY YOURSELF?

247
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,178
HE HOOKED UP.

248
00:09:56,513 --> 00:09:58,473
HE HOOKED UP
WITH SOMEONE.

249
00:09:58,515 --> 00:10:01,184
LOOK, I DON'T HAVE TO ANSWER
YOUR QUESTIONS, OKAY?

250
00:10:01,226 --> 00:10:03,437
I'M A BIG BOY.
I CAN DO WHATEVER I WANT.

251
00:10:03,478 --> 00:10:04,896
HE HOOKED UP.

252
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:09,650
TELL US ABOUT HER.

253
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:11,403
ROSS, YOU LET YOUR SCARF IN...

254
00:10:18,577 --> 00:10:19,702
HEY, YOU GUYS.

255
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:21,580
( horselike giggles )

256
00:10:28,962 --> 00:10:31,089
O-O-OKAY. OKAY.

257
00:10:31,131 --> 00:10:33,425
I KNOW WHAT YOU ALL
ARE THINKING

258
00:10:33,467 --> 00:10:35,260
BUT CHANDLER IS IN YEMEN.

259
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:39,013
I'M A YOUNG WOMAN.
I HAVE NEEDS.

260
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,348
I CAN'T WAIT FOREVER.

261
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:42,559
YEAH, NO, THAT'S
WHAT I WAS THINKING.

262
00:10:44,436 --> 00:10:46,187
SO I'M ASKING YOU, PLEASE

263
00:10:46,229 --> 00:10:48,898
JUST TAKE A MOMENT
BEFORE YOU JUDGE ME.

264
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:50,442
OH, NOBODY'S
JUDGING YOU.

265
00:10:50,484 --> 00:10:52,693
OH. OKAY.

266
00:10:52,735 --> 00:10:56,448
YOU, MR. "RIGHT PLACE
AT THE RIGHT TIME..."

267
00:10:58,408 --> 00:10:59,451
CALL ME.

268
00:10:59,493 --> 00:11:01,661
( braying laughter )

269
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:11,087
OKAY, LOOK, I KNOW
WHAT YOU GUYS ARE GOING TO SAY.

270
00:11:11,129 --> 00:11:14,466
YOU TWO WOULD HAVE
VERY HAIRY CHILDREN.

271
00:11:14,508 --> 00:11:17,511
OKAY, I DIDN'T KNOW
YOU WOULD SAY THAT.

272
00:11:17,552 --> 00:11:20,555
ROSS? JANICE?

273
00:11:20,597 --> 00:11:21,556
ALL RIGHT, HOLD ON.

274
00:11:21,598 --> 00:11:22,557
HOLD ON. HOLD ON.

275
00:11:22,599 --> 00:11:23,682
THIS IS ROSS.

276
00:11:23,724 --> 00:11:24,683
OKAY?

277
00:11:24,725 --> 00:11:25,935
HE'S OUR FRIEND.

278
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:27,686
HE OBVIOUSLY
WENT CRAZY.

279
00:11:27,728 --> 00:11:29,648
HE OBVIOUSLY
LOST HIS MIND.

280
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:31,816
NO, I DIDN'T LOSE MY MIND.

281
00:11:31,858 --> 00:11:35,069
OKAY? JANICE AND I
HAVE A LOT IN COMMON.

282
00:11:35,111 --> 00:11:37,447
WE'VE...
WE'VE BOTH BEEN DIVORCED.

283
00:11:37,489 --> 00:11:39,199
WE... WE BOTH HAVE KIDS.

284
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:41,326
SO ARE YOU ACTUALLY
GOING TO SEE HER AGAIN?

285
00:11:41,368 --> 00:11:43,328
PHOEBE, DON'T PUT
IDEAS IN HIS HEAD.

286
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:44,996
I AM GOING
TO SEE HER AGAIN.

287
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:46,581
DAMN IT, PHOEBE!

288
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:52,003
OKAY, I HAVE
TO TELL YOU SOMETHING

289
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:54,673
THAT I'VE NEVER ADMITTED
THROUGHOUT OUR ENTIRE FRIENDSHIP

290
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:56,049
BUT WHEN WE WERE
IN HIGH SCHOOL

291
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:57,258
I MADE OUT
WITH JAMES FARROW

292
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:58,926
EVEN THOUGH I KNEW
THAT YOU LIKED HIM.

293
00:11:58,968 --> 00:12:00,845
WOW, THAT FEELS SO GOOD
TO GET OFF MY CHEST.

294
00:12:00,887 --> 00:12:01,846
OKAY, YOU GO.

295
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:02,972
MY TURN?

296
00:12:03,014 --> 00:12:05,933
W-WHAT ARE YOU
TALKING ABOUT?

297
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:10,397
MONICA... I KNOW
ABOUT YOU AND CHANDLER.

298
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:12,524
WHAT?

299
00:12:12,566 --> 00:12:15,235
I OVERHEARD YOU GUYS
ON THE PHONE THE OTHER DAY

300
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,320
AND YOU SAID,
"I'LL JUST TELL RACHEL

301
00:12:17,362 --> 00:12:19,989
THAT I'M DOING LAUNDRY
FOR A COUPLE OF HOURS."

302
00:12:20,031 --> 00:12:22,783
AND HE SAID, "LAUNDRY?
"IS THAT MY NEW NICKNAME?"

303
00:12:22,825 --> 00:12:24,869
AND YOU SAID, "NO.

304
00:12:24,911 --> 00:12:29,123
YOU KNOW WHAT YOUR NICKNAME IS,
MR. BIG."

305
00:12:33,211 --> 00:12:35,922
WELL... SOUNDS LIKE
YOU'RE WRITING YOURSELF

306
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,674
A LITTLE PLAY
THERE, RACH.

307
00:12:39,217 --> 00:12:42,303
WOW, I... LET ME KNOW
HOW THAT ONE TURNS OUT.

308
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:43,722
WELL, I WOULDN'T KNOW

309
00:12:43,762 --> 00:12:47,016
BECAUSE I GOT SO FREAKED OUT
I HUNG UP THE PHONE.

310
00:12:47,058 --> 00:12:49,977
WELL, IF YOU HAD
KEPT LISTENING

311
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:54,691
Y-YOU WOULD HAVE HEARD
ME CALL HIM MR. BIG... IT.

312
00:12:54,733 --> 00:12:55,692
WHAT?

313
00:12:55,734 --> 00:12:57,652
MR. BIGOT.

314
00:12:57,694 --> 00:12:59,112
I MEAN....

315
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:02,657
HE TELLS THE
MOST RACIST JOKES.

316
00:13:02,699 --> 00:13:04,618
ALL RIGHT. SO THAT'S IT?

317
00:13:04,659 --> 00:13:07,954
YOU'RE TELLING ME
THERE'S NOTHING GOING ON

318
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:09,997
BETWEEN YOU AND CHANDLER?

319
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:11,708
ME AND CHANDLER?

320
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:13,543
( work laughter )

321
00:13:16,671 --> 00:13:18,590
ALL RIGHT, PUT
YOUR 20 BUCKS DOWN.

322
00:13:18,632 --> 00:13:20,675
FIRST ONE TO FIND THE
TASTY TREAT WINS. OKAY?

323
00:13:20,717 --> 00:13:21,676
MM-HMM.

324
00:13:21,718 --> 00:13:23,344
ALL RIGHT.

325
00:13:23,386 --> 00:13:27,265
LET'S GET THE CONTESTANTS
OUT OF THEIR ISOLATION BOOTHS.

326
00:13:27,307 --> 00:13:28,933
AND THEY'RE OFF.

327
00:13:28,975 --> 00:13:30,435
OH...

328
00:13:30,477 --> 00:13:32,811
GET YOUR FOOT OFF
MY CONTESTANT. JUDGE?

329
00:13:32,853 --> 00:13:34,939
JUDGE RULES
NO VIOLATION.

330
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:36,274
( sighing )

331
00:13:36,316 --> 00:13:37,816
HEY, GUYS.

332
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:39,944
HEY.
YEAH.

333
00:13:39,986 --> 00:13:42,155
YOU KNOW WHAT?
IT'S SO WEIRD TO SAY THIS

334
00:13:42,196 --> 00:13:44,407
BUT I JUST HAD
A GREAT DATE WITH JANICE.

335
00:13:44,449 --> 00:13:45,408
WHAT?

336
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:47,076
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

337
00:13:47,118 --> 00:13:49,996
YEAH. I OPENED UP TO HER
ABOUT ALL THE TERRIBLE STUFF

338
00:13:50,037 --> 00:13:51,581
THAT'S BEEN HAPPENING TO ME.

339
00:13:51,623 --> 00:13:53,207
I MEAN, I TALKED FOR HOURS.

340
00:13:53,249 --> 00:13:54,875
IT IS AMAZING

341
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:58,296
TO HAVE SOMEONE GIVE YOU
SUCH... SUCH FOCUSED ATTENTION.

342
00:13:58,338 --> 00:14:00,423
YOU DON'T NEED
JANICE FOR THAT.

343
00:14:00,465 --> 00:14:01,466
YOU'VE GOT US.

344
00:14:01,508 --> 00:14:03,468
THE DUCK GETS
A NUTTER BUTTER.

345
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:04,719
EEW! OH, HEY,
THAT'S NOT

346
00:14:04,761 --> 00:14:05,886
A NUTTER BUTTER.

347
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:07,972
THAT'S JUST
AN OLD WONTON.

348
00:14:08,014 --> 00:14:09,140
JUDGE RULES...

349
00:14:09,182 --> 00:14:10,433
NUTTER BUTTER.

350
00:14:10,475 --> 00:14:11,850
( groaning )

351
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:13,144
TOUGH CALL.
YEAH.

352
00:14:15,355 --> 00:14:17,023
( laughter )

353
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:19,233
BUT, SERIOUSLY,
I STRONGLY BELIEVE

354
00:14:19,275 --> 00:14:22,111
THAT WE SHOULD ALL SUPPORT
PRESIDENT CLINTON

355
00:14:22,153 --> 00:14:23,488
AND HER HUSBAND, BILL.

356
00:14:23,530 --> 00:14:26,866
( guys laughing obnoxiously )

357
00:14:26,907 --> 00:14:29,035
SO, HOW DO YOU KIDS
LIKE YOUR COFFEE?

358
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:30,161
OH, NONE FOR
ME, THANKS.

359
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:31,245
A LITTLE BIT
OF SUGAR.

360
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:32,497
I'LL BRING IT OUT

361
00:14:32,539 --> 00:14:33,998
AND HAVE MONICA
STICK HER FINGER IN IT.

362
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:34,999
THAT'LL SWEETEN IT UP.

363
00:14:35,041 --> 00:14:37,418
( guys laughing )

364
00:14:39,337 --> 00:14:41,339
HOW DOES THAT LAUGH
NOT GIVE YOU A HEADACHE?

365
00:14:41,381 --> 00:14:42,507
OH, YOU GET USED TO IT.

366
00:14:42,549 --> 00:14:43,633
I-I DON'T THINK
THAT I CAN

367
00:14:43,675 --> 00:14:45,051
SO, IF YOU DON'T MIND

368
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:46,845
MAYBE THIS WILL BE IT
FOR ME ON THE WORK THINGS.

369
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:48,304
SO I LAUGH AT MY BOSS'S JOKES.

370
00:14:48,346 --> 00:14:49,472
WHAT'S THE BIG DEAL?

371
00:14:49,514 --> 00:14:50,640
I'D RATHER NOT HANG OUT

372
00:14:50,682 --> 00:14:52,600
WITH THIS SNIVELING,
WORK-WEASEL GUY

373
00:14:52,642 --> 00:14:55,687
WHEN I COULD BE HANGING
OUT WITH MY BOYFRIEND,
WHO I ACTUALLY RESPECT.

374
00:14:55,729 --> 00:14:57,230
OH.

375
00:14:58,439 --> 00:15:01,693
AH. I GOT TO APOLOGIZE
FOR KARA'S COFFEE, YOU KNOW?

376
00:15:01,735 --> 00:15:04,529
FEEL SORRY FOR IT
IF IT EVER GOT IN A FIGHT.

377
00:15:04,571 --> 00:15:06,406
IT'S NOT STRONG ENOUGH
TO DEFEND ITSELF.

378
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:07,615
( laughing )

379
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:10,034
( laughter
tapers off )

380
00:15:11,494 --> 00:15:12,995
DID YOU HEAR WHAT I SAID, BING?

381
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:15,122
WHAT?

382
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:16,416
IT'S A JOKE, BING.

383
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,418
WHAT'S THE MATTER WITH YOU?

384
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:21,713
WELL, I-I, I JUST DIDN'T THINK
IT WAS FUNNY, SIR.

385
00:15:21,755 --> 00:15:22,963
EXCUSE ME?

386
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:24,591
WELL, I-I JUST...

387
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:29,178
HONEY, I JUST DON'T
THINK THAT YOU
UNDERSTOOD THE JOKE.

388
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:30,388
REALLY?

389
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:31,765
YEAH. I MEAN...

390
00:15:31,806 --> 00:15:33,057
IT WAS REALLY FUNNY.

391
00:15:33,099 --> 00:15:35,309
I JUST DON'T THINK
THAT YOU GOT IT.

392
00:15:35,351 --> 00:15:38,605
YOU SEE, KARA'S COFFEE
IS, IS, IS WEAK TASTING

393
00:15:38,646 --> 00:15:41,232
OKAY, BUT WHAT DOUG
DID WAS TO IMPLY

394
00:15:41,274 --> 00:15:43,276
THAT IT WAS WEAK
PHYSICALLY.

395
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:46,696
YOU GET IT
NOW, HONEY?

396
00:15:46,738 --> 00:15:47,906
I THINK I DO.

397
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,031
( both laughing obnoxiously )

398
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:52,368
( Doug joins in )

399
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:53,912
THANK YOU, MONICA.

400
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:55,705
I THOUGHT YOU COULD
USE THE HELP.

401
00:15:57,081 --> 00:15:58,875
COFFEE IN A FIGHT!

402
00:15:58,917 --> 00:16:00,627
( both laughing )

403
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,589
HEY, RACH.

404
00:16:04,631 --> 00:16:06,966
DO YOU MIND IF I READ
MY COMIC BOOKS IN HERE?

405
00:16:08,927 --> 00:16:10,969
SURE. WHY?

406
00:16:11,011 --> 00:16:11,971
OH, WELL

407
00:16:12,012 --> 00:16:13,347
CHANDLER AND MONICA
ARE OVER THERE

408
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:15,850
AND, YOU KNOW, IT'S KIND OF HARD
TO CONCENTRATE.

409
00:16:15,892 --> 00:16:17,310
WHAT?! SHE JUST CALLED

410
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:20,480
AND SAID THAT SHE WAS GOING
TO BE WORKING LATE.

411
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:22,398
OKAY, SHE KEEPS LYING
TO ME.

412
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,566
THAT'S IT. YOU KNOW WHAT?

413
00:16:23,608 --> 00:16:24,859
I'M GOING TO GO OVER THERE

414
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:26,486
AND I'M CONFRONTING THEM
RIGHT NOW.

415
00:16:37,121 --> 00:16:39,540
Chandler:
ALL RIGHT,
SO YOU'RE TELLING ME

416
00:16:39,582 --> 00:16:41,793
THAT I HAVE TO TELL
RACIST JOKES NOW?

417
00:16:41,835 --> 00:16:44,545
Monica:
I'M SORRY.
I'M NOT VERY GOOD AT THIS.

418
00:16:44,587 --> 00:16:45,839
I'M A TERRIBLE LIAR

419
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:47,590
AND I HATE HAVING
TO LIE TO RACHEL.

420
00:16:47,632 --> 00:16:49,425
YEAH, BUT WE'RE NOT READY
TO TELL YET.

421
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:50,885
I KNOW. IT'S JUST THAT

422
00:16:50,927 --> 00:16:53,429
EVER SINCE HIGH SCHOOL,
RACHEL WAS THE ONE PERSON

423
00:16:53,471 --> 00:16:55,431
THAT I TOLD
EVERYTHING
TO, YOU KNOW?

424
00:16:55,473 --> 00:16:57,767
I MISS THAT
SO MUCH NOW.

425
00:16:57,809 --> 00:16:59,978
SHE'S MY BEST FRIEND.

426
00:17:03,815 --> 00:17:05,274
( gasping )

427
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,902
JOEY?

428
00:17:09,278 --> 00:17:10,947
OH, MY GOD. RACHEL.

429
00:17:10,989 --> 00:17:12,907
HEY! HI!

430
00:17:12,949 --> 00:17:16,410
W-W-W-WHAT,
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

431
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:18,538
WELL, I WAS ACTUALLY...

432
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:22,124
I CAME OVER HERE
TO BORROW THIS LAMP...

433
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:24,961
TO, UM, LOOK AT MY BOOKS,
YOU KNOW?

434
00:17:25,003 --> 00:17:26,963
SEE 'EM A LITTLE BETTER.

435
00:17:27,005 --> 00:17:31,843
OKAY, GREAT. GREAT. UM...

436
00:17:31,885 --> 00:17:34,303
W-WHAT I WAS DOING
IN CHANDLER'S ROOM

437
00:17:34,345 --> 00:17:36,848
IS THAT, UM, WELL,
I WAS CLEANING IT.

438
00:17:36,890 --> 00:17:38,057
OH.

439
00:17:38,098 --> 00:17:39,976
IN FACT, HE PAYS ME TO CLEAN IT.

440
00:17:40,018 --> 00:17:44,898
OH! WHAT A, YOU KNOW, GREAT WAY
TO MAKE SOME EXTRA POCKET MONEY.

441
00:17:44,939 --> 00:17:47,817
YEAH. YOU KNOW,
WHEN I SAID TO YOU EARLIER

442
00:17:47,859 --> 00:17:49,610
THAT I WAS AT WORK, UM...

443
00:17:49,652 --> 00:17:50,987
I'M AT MY NEW WORK.

444
00:17:51,029 --> 00:17:54,615
GOOD ENOUGH. RIGHT?

445
00:17:54,657 --> 00:17:57,535
OKAY, WELL, UM...

446
00:17:57,577 --> 00:17:59,370
I'M GOING
TO GO LOOK AT MY BOOKS.

447
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:00,663
OKAY.

448
00:18:00,705 --> 00:18:01,831
OKAY.

449
00:18:01,873 --> 00:18:03,875
GO GET BACK TO MY NEW JOB.

450
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:06,836
OKAY.

451
00:18:09,547 --> 00:18:12,383
CONGRATULATIONS
ON YOUR NEW JOB.

452
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:16,888
( door opens
and shuts )

453
00:18:19,223 --> 00:18:20,975
MAN, SHE IS
REALLY GULLIBLE.

454
00:18:21,017 --> 00:18:22,643
( whistling )

455
00:18:27,565 --> 00:18:28,691
HERE YOU GO.

456
00:18:28,733 --> 00:18:29,817
OH, THANKS.

457
00:18:29,859 --> 00:18:31,527
ACTUALLY, I
SHOULD GET GOING.

458
00:18:31,569 --> 00:18:32,820
OH, Y-YOU SURE?

459
00:18:32,862 --> 00:18:35,031
BECAUSE I CAN STAY OUT
AS LATE AS YOU WANT.

460
00:18:35,073 --> 00:18:37,408
I TOLD YOU HOW I'M ON SABBATICAL
FROM WORK, RIGHT?

461
00:18:37,450 --> 00:18:38,534
YES, YES, YOU DID.

462
00:18:38,576 --> 00:18:39,702
( laughing )

463
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:41,203
( whining ):
OH, MAN!

464
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:43,121
WHAT IS WRONG NOW?

465
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:45,708
THIS ISN'T WHAT I ORDERED!

466
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:49,670
MAN, CAN'T ANYTHING
GO RIGHT IN MY LIFE?!

467
00:18:49,712 --> 00:18:53,967
FIRST MY MARRIAGE FALLS APART,
AND THEN I...

468
00:18:54,008 --> 00:18:55,593
I KNOW, I KNOW!

469
00:18:55,635 --> 00:18:57,344
AND THEN YOU LOSE
YOUR APARTMENT

470
00:18:57,386 --> 00:18:58,805
AND THEN YOU LOSE YOUR JOB

471
00:18:58,846 --> 00:19:01,139
AND THEN YOUR EX-WIFE
GETS MARRIED SO FAST

472
00:19:01,181 --> 00:19:02,683
AND NOW THE COFFEE... AAH!

473
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:05,394
ROSS.

474
00:19:05,436 --> 00:19:06,938
WE NEED TO TALK.

475
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:09,356
OKAY.
SOMETIMES I FEEL...

476
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:11,776
NO-NO-NO-NO, NO, NO.

477
00:19:11,818 --> 00:19:14,737
I'M GOING TO TALK.

478
00:19:14,779 --> 00:19:21,159
I BELIEVE THAT THE
SUN HAS SET ON OUR...

479
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:22,787
DAY IN THE SUN.

480
00:19:23,830 --> 00:19:25,081
WHAT?

481
00:19:25,123 --> 00:19:29,752
YOU'RE A VERY SWEET
PERSON, ROSS... UM...

482
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:33,798
UNFORTUNATELY, I
JUST DON'T THINK

483
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:37,135
I CAN TAKE ANOTHER
SECOND OF YOU WHINING!

484
00:19:39,929 --> 00:19:44,100
UH, LET ME MAKE SURE
I'M HEARING THIS RIGHT. YOU...

485
00:19:44,142 --> 00:19:47,269
YOU'RE ENDING THIS WITH ME

486
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:49,939
BECAUSE I'M TOO WHINY?

487
00:19:49,981 --> 00:19:51,816
MMM.

488
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:55,153
SO, YOU'RE SAYING

489
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:58,489
I'VE BECOME SO WHINY

490
00:19:58,531 --> 00:20:00,616
THAT I

491
00:20:00,658 --> 00:20:04,162
ANNOY YOU.

492
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:06,205
JANICE.

493
00:20:06,246 --> 00:20:07,832
WELL, YEAH!

494
00:20:07,874 --> 00:20:12,003
OH. MY. GOD.

495
00:20:12,045 --> 00:20:14,630
ARE YOU GOING TO BE OKAY?

496
00:20:14,672 --> 00:20:16,674
I AM NOW.

497
00:20:16,716 --> 00:20:18,384
OKAY.

498
00:20:21,971 --> 00:20:24,140
UH... HI.

499
00:20:24,182 --> 00:20:25,349
OH, HI.

500
00:20:25,391 --> 00:20:28,186
WELL...

501
00:20:28,226 --> 00:20:31,189
I GUESS
THAT'S TWO OUT OF THREE.

502
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:32,356
JOEY.

503
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:33,733
( braying laugh )

504
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:44,535
DUDE, WE GOT TO TALK.

505
00:20:44,577 --> 00:20:46,120
OKAY.

506
00:20:46,162 --> 00:20:48,164
I JUST WANTED TO
TELL YOU SOMETHING

507
00:20:48,206 --> 00:20:50,374
BEFORE YOU HEARD IT
FROM SOMEONE ELSE

508
00:20:50,416 --> 00:20:52,210
AND I HOPE THIS
ISN'T TOO WEIRD

509
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:53,836
BUT, UH...

510
00:20:53,878 --> 00:20:57,965
I HAD A-A THING WITH JANICE.

511
00:20:58,007 --> 00:21:01,385
( cracking up )

512
00:21:01,427 --> 00:21:04,263
WHAT, YOU'RE, YOU'RE NOT MAD?

513
00:21:04,304 --> 00:21:05,765
WHY WOULD I BE MAD?

514
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:08,142
WELL, BECAUSE, YOU KNOW,
THERE ARE CERTAIN RULES

515
00:21:08,184 --> 00:21:09,435
ABOUT THIS KIND OF STUFF.

516
00:21:09,476 --> 00:21:11,311
YOU DON'T, UH,
YOU DON'T FOOL AROUND

517
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:12,980
WITH YOUR FRIENDS'
EX-GIRLFRIENDS

518
00:21:13,022 --> 00:21:14,607
OR, UH

519
00:21:14,648 --> 00:21:17,610
POSSIBLE GIRLFRIENDS,
OR GIRLS THEY'RE RELATED TO.

520
00:21:22,531 --> 00:21:24,575
I AM MAD.

521
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:27,912
BUT YOU KNOW
WHAT I'M GONNA DO?

522
00:21:27,954 --> 00:21:31,124
I'M GONNA FORGIVE YOU,
BECAUSE THAT'S WHAT FRIENDS DO.

523
00:21:31,165 --> 00:21:32,332
THEY FORGIVE THEIR FRIENDS

524
00:21:32,374 --> 00:21:34,001
WHEN THEY DO
EVERYTHING YOU JUST SAID.

525
00:21:34,043 --> 00:21:35,502
ALL THE THINGS
ON THE LIST THERE.

526
00:21:35,544 --> 00:21:37,088
THANK YOU.
WELL

527
00:21:37,130 --> 00:21:41,508
BUT I WANT YOU TO REMEMBER
THAT I FORGAVE YOU.

528
00:21:42,635 --> 00:21:44,011
OKAY.

529
00:21:44,053 --> 00:21:45,763
I ALSO WANT YOU TO REMEMBER

530
00:21:45,805 --> 00:21:48,015
THAT I LET YOU LIVE HERE
RENT FREE.

531
00:21:48,057 --> 00:21:49,725
ALL RIGHT.

532
00:21:49,767 --> 00:21:55,606
AND I WANT YOU TO REMEMBER
THAT I GAVE YOU $27.

533
00:21:56,816 --> 00:21:58,192
NO STRINGS ATTACHED.

534
00:21:58,234 --> 00:21:59,693
IF YOU CAN'T
REMEMBER THAT

535
00:21:59,735 --> 00:22:01,904
I THINK WE SHOULD WRITE IT DOWN.
LET'S WRITE IT DOWN.

536
00:22:01,946 --> 00:22:05,825
